  rankdir="TB";
  "I_Coupling" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-Reasoning: Reducing coupling suppresses loss (S19) and coupling reflects vibrations (S18), so understanding coupling is vital."];
  "I_Morph" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-Reasoning: Morphology affects FF (S8) and synergistic improvement is key (S9), so morphology optimization is crucial."];
  "I_Problem" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-Reasoning: OSCs have higher loss (S3) and minimizing loss is essential (S4), so there is a critical problem to solve."];
  "I_Stacking" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-Reasoning: Side chains modulate stacking (S13) and branching alters stacking (S14), so side chain design controls stacking."];
  "I_Status" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-Reasoning: OSCs are promising (S1) and PCE is high (S2), so the field is active and viable."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes to investigate asymmetric alkyl/thienyl outer side chains in A-DA'D-A small-molecule acceptors for PM6-based organic solar cells, testing whether such design promotes backbone planarization, denser molecular packing, reduced electron-vibrational and non-radiative losses, improved exciton dissociation and charge transport, and ultimately higher power-conversion efficiency.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When OSC performance is limited by non-radiative and electron-vibrational losses, and side-chain structure influences stacking, morphology, and coupling-relevant intermolecular interactions, asymmetric acceptor design becomes a coherent research route to test performance improvements."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Asymmetric side-chain acceptor designs warrant investigation for their effects on morphology, stacking-related packing, loss, and photovoltaic performance."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) Introducing luminescent moieties can support the high-photoluminescence component of strategies for minimizing voltage losses, while low energy offset remains an additional required factor."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Because side-chain design can control molecular stacking, it provides a plausible structural handle for manipulating intermolecular interactions relevant to electron-vibrational coupling and loss."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) A reported asymmetric molecule with less energy loss, together with the broader role of side-chain design in controlling stacking, motivates investigating asymmetric side-chain designs as a strategy rather than proving asymmetry is generally valid."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) Because OSCs are promising yet limited by high energy loss and the need to minimize non-radiative voltage loss, further research aimed at reducing losses is well motivated."];
  "S1" [label="(1,0,0) OSCs have merits (lightness, flexibility) and are promising green energy technologies."];
  "S10" [label="(10,0,0) Manipulating intermolecular interactions controls coupling to suppress loss and improve FF."];
  "S13" [label="(13,0,0) Side chain modifications modulate solubility, crystallization, and stacking behavior."];
  "S14" [label="(14,0,0) Different positions of alkyl-chain-branching alter molecular stacking and phase separation."];
  "S17" [label="(17,0,0) Asymmetric molecules (e.g., A-C10ch) demonstrated less energy loss than symmetric ones."];
  "S18" [label="(18,0,0) Electron-vibrational coupling reflects interactions between electrons and intramolecular vibrations."];
  "S19" [label="(19,0,0) Reducing electron-vibrational coupling suppresses non-radiative recombination and loss."];
  "S2" [label="(2,0,0) Advances in SMAs have pushed single junction OSC PCE beyond 19%."];
  "S3" [label="(3,0,0) OSCs have higher energy loss and lower FF compared to inorganic technologies."];
  "S4" [label="(4,0,0) Minimizing non-radiative voltage loss is essential for enhancing Voc and properties."];
  "S6" [label="(6,0,0) Low energy offset and high PL yield are key factors for minimizing voltage losses."];
  "S7" [label="(7,0,0) Introducing luminescent moieties enhances rigidity and achieves high PL molecules."];
  "S8" [label="(8,0,0) Film morphology is closely related to charge transport, FF, and efficiency."];
  "S9" [label="(9,0,0) Synergistically improving luminescence and morphology is key but challenging."];
